# Build context for deploy/Dockerfile, which builds from the repository root because it needs
# api/, web/ and db/ together. Without this file that context includes ai/ -- whose image
# bakes ~2.8 GB of models -- and every node_modules and vendor directory on disk, all of which
# are sent to the daemon before the first instruction runs.

.git
.gitignore
.claude

# Not part of the production image at all: deploy/Dockerfile ships the API and the built SPA,
# and deliberately not the two Python services. Their models will not fit in a free tier's
# memory, and deploy/README.md has what to set to get transcription from a hosted provider
# instead.
ai/

# Rebuilt inside the image by `npm ci` and `composer install`. Copying the host's copies in
# would be slower *and* wrong -- they are built for the host's platform, and node_modules
# carries compiled binaries that may not match the image's architecture.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
api/vendor/

# Development-only, and each would change the built image if it leaked in.
api/tests/
api/phpunit.xml
api/.env
api/.env.*
docker-compose.yml
.env
.env.*

# Notes and documentation. Large, and read by people rather than by the runtime.
NOTES.md
README.md

**/.DS_Store
